{"id":"rel.wave2.batch35.01.integral-over-ideal.to.two-sided-ideal","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.integral-over-ideal","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.two-sided-ideal","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"I⊆R be an ideal","editorial_reason":"The defining integrality-over-I polynomial uses a specified ideal I of R and coefficient powers I^{d−j}. A commutative ring ideal has the general two-sided ideal axioms as prerequisite; the additional coefficient restrictions remain essential.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/037E","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AIdeal_of_Ring","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_stacks_embedded_definitions_prerequisite_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch35.02.integral-over-ideal.to.ring-map-unital","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.integral-over-ideal","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.ring-map-unital","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"homomorphism of commutative rings","editorial_reason":"The definition is relative to a homomorphism φ:R→S of commutative rings. In the Stacks unital-ring convention, the independently screened unital ring homomorphism supplies the map preserving both operations and 1; the coefficient-power condition is additional.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/037E","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_Homomorphism","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_stacks_embedded_definitions_prerequisite_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch35.03.local-ring-fibre-at-prime.to.ring-map-unital","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.local-ring-fibre-at-prime","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.ring-map-unital","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"homomorphism of commutative rings","editorial_reason":"A fibre ring S⊗_Rκ(p) and the local quotient S_q/pS_q require a commutative unital ring map R→S. The independent unital ring-map meaning supplies that prerequisite without claiming every map is flat or finite.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OG","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_Homomorphism","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_stacks_embedded_definitions_prerequisite_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch35.04.local-ring-fibre-at-prime.to.commutative-prime-ideal","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.local-ring-fibre-at-prime","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.commutative-prime-ideal","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"prime ideal q⊆S","editorial_reason":"The local ring of the fibre at q is defined only after choosing a prime q of S and its contraction p in R; the general proper prime-ideal property is a prerequisite, not a residue-field definition.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OG","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3APrime_Ideal_of_Ring/Commutative_and_Unitary_Ring","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_stacks_embedded_definitions_prerequisite_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch35.05.local-ring-fibre-at-prime.to.ring-localization-at-multiplicative-set","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.local-ring-fibre-at-prime","target_meaning":"meaning.70f44988651b76b5.ring-localization-at-multiplicative-set","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"localization of the fibre ring","editorial_reason":"Stacks Definition 10.112.5 uses localization of the fibre ring at the prime corresponding to q (equivalently S_q/pS_q). General commutative ring localization is prerequisite, while quotient formation and κ(p) remain separately unsourced foundational concepts.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OG","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00CM","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_stacks_embedded_definitions_prerequisite_review_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
